xt-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the most popular endangered species names for pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Tiger, Panda, Cheetah, and Snow Leopard are consistently popular choices. Koala and Red Panda have surged in recent years. Marine-inspired names like Dolphin, Sea Turtle, and Blue Whale are also widely used. These names work well because they're recognizable, easy to pronounce, and carry positive associations.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I name my pet after an endangered animal that doesn't match their species?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. A cat named Panda or a dog named Tiger is both common and charming. There's no rule that names must match the species — in fact, the contrast can be delightful. The name carries meaning regardless of what animal wears it.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are there regional endangered species names worth considering?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes. Consider naming your pet after a species local to your region — it strengthens your connection to local conservation efforts. For example, a California Condor for a bird, a Florida Panther for a cat, or an Iberian Lynx for Spanish-speaking pet owners. These regional names add a personal, place-based dimension.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How can naming my pet help endangered species awareness?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"When someone asks about your pet's unusual name, you have a natural opportunity to share information about the real endangered animal. 'Her name is Saola — it's one of the rarest mammals on Earth' often leads to meaningful conversations. Over a pet's lifetime, that name can spark hundreds of awareness-raising moments.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are some lesser-known endangered species with beautiful names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Many rare species have lyrical names perfect for pets: Quokka (a smiling marsupial), Saola (the 'Asian unicorn'), Vaquita (the world's rarest marine mammal), Kakapo (a flightless parrot), Dhole (an Asian wild dog), and Pangolin (a scaled mammal). These names are unique, beautiful, and rich with meaning.\"}]]}],\"$L3c\"]}]]}]\n37:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"tiger\",{\"href\":\"/animal/tiger/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐯\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Tiger\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"elephant\",{\"href\":\"/animal/elephant/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-